Benthoclast

Ingredients: INDUSTRIAL ROCK / METAL + TRIPPY, SURREAL & PSYCHEDELIC + Bongos + 2010s ERA  
Creative Catalyst: The sound was discovered by deep-sea commercial divers repairing transatlantic fiber-optic data cables beneath four thousand meters of crushing hydrostatic pressure.

Benthoclast is a claustrophobic, hyper-pressurized collision of abrasive industrial metal and disorienting hyperbaric psychedelia. Instead of acoustic campfire percussion or Latin syncopation, high-tension ceramic bongos are slammed with lead-weighted diver gauntlets to drive frantic, subterranean polyrhythms beneath detuned, baritone seven-string sludge. The early-2010s era wall-of-sound production—reminiscent of peak brickwall mastering, sidechained sub-bass blasts, and glitchy digital clipping—is plunged underwater, saturated in nitrogen-narcosis delirium, oceanic hum, and eerie transcontinental data packet screeching.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 78–110 BPM. Sluggish, lumbering industrial march tempos counterbalanced by dizzying, hyperspeed quintuplet and septuplet rolls hammered on high-pressure tuned bongos, mimicking mechanical seabed drillers and erratic fiber-optic packet jitter.
- Harmonic Palette: Dissonant Locrian and Phrygian dominant modalities layered over cavernous drop-F# bass drones; shifting microtonal flurries simulate nitrogen narcosis and Doppler-warped oceanic sonar.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Hydrobaric Cavitation Crunch: Sub-bass frequencies and chugging power chords routed through submerged speaker drivers and captured via hydrophones, creating implosive low-end thuds without room reverberation.
  2. Deep-Strand Transduction: An impossible studio method where raw multi-track audio is fired as laser light through coiled, salt-corroded optical fibers kept under 6,000 PSI in hyperbaric chambers, introducing strange crystalline phase artifacts, glass refraction chirps, and jittery packet-loss distortion.
  3. Brickwall Sieve Gating: Aggressive 2010s-style sidechain ducking where thick wall-of-sound industrial riffs violently yield whenever the high-frequency bongos strike, giving the listener the physiological sensation of inner-ear barotrauma and fluctuating lung pressure.
- Dynamics: Songs start in suffocating, dead-weight silence with only the pinging chatter of fiber cables and bongo skin taps, erupting without warning into catastrophic, hydro-sheared industrial metal explosions before dissolving into hallucinogenic, bioluminescent ambient drifts.

Scene & Origin Lore
Benthoclast was born in 2014 in the cramped decompression habitats and saturation diving barges idling over the Porcupine Abyssal Plain. Technicians and commercial deep-sea welders spent weeks in pressurized helium-oxygen atmospheres repairing transatlantic telecommunication lines. Down there, exposed severed cables hummed with millions of terabytes of encrypted global communications, vibrating directly against their diving helmets with an intoxicating, metallic pulse. Upon surfacing, divers dragged spare titanium cable sheaths and ceramic test drums into coastal fish-smoking sheds and shipyard storage hulls across Reykjavik, Brest, and Halifax. The emerging subculture rejected standard industrial goth fashion; followers wore grease-smeared neoprene immersion suits, diver knives strapped to calves, high-visibility orange foul-weather bibs, and modified umbilical communication headsets. Their concerts—held inside wet-docks and flooded ballast tanks—operate like high-pressure galley kitchens: performers cook massive pots of salted tallow and fish stew on kerosene stoves beside the stage, sharing communal broth with the audience while rhythmic clatter and down-tuned roar simulate the crushing weight of the Atlantic floor.

Typical Instruments
- Primary Percussion: Ceramic-and-carbon-fiber bongos fitted with hydrophones, struck with brass knuckles, steel mallets, and weighted diver mittens.
- Heavy Strings: Drop-tuned 8-string guitars with rusted steel strings, channeled through custom-built bass amps caked in marine epoxy.
- Synths & Electronics: 2010s-era wavetable software synthesizers, bitcrushed hydrophone field recordings, marine sonar pings, piezoelectric transducers clamped to live copper wire.
- Vocals: Dual-channel dry breathing-mask growls layered with hyper-processed helium-shift screams and muttered saturation dive-logs.

For Fans Of: Author & Punisher, Nine Inch Nails, Swans, Godflesh

