Track 3: Phase-Inversion Braise
- Story & Context: In the winter of 2017, the coastal community of Hvalfjörður gathered inside an offshore cable terminus to salvage forty miles of abandoned copper-core wiring by boiling the outer vulcanized tar in an enormous galvanized steel soup cauldron. Soundman Aris Thorne lowered contact hydrophones and piezos directly into the bubbling black pitch, feeding the boiling thuds through a cranked 2012 digital limiter while three local drummers battered a manic bongo counterpoint atop the vat's iron rims. As the resulting broadcast overloaded the regional harbor radio, Thorne screamed the final rite into the steam: "Skim the grease off the signal and swallow the hum."
